    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite score of 86.26, fueled by an excellent matchup against Zack Littell. While the stolen base suppression from a strong-armed opponent hurts his floor slightly, his position in the #3 hole and the favorable park factors make him a must-start. **Josh Naylor** also warrants high confidence (78.46) as he exploits a soft matchup against Keider Montero; the wind blowing out significantly elevates his HR potential, making him a prime candidate for power production. **James Wood** stands as another cornerstone play at 75.08, benefiting from an elite xwOBA profile and a high-leverage leadoff spot that projects him for multiple run-scoring opportunities.\n\nPlatoon advantages are driving several of our mid-tier decisions, most notably for **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Jose Caballero**. Despite Joe Ryan being a formidable arm, **Vinnie Pasquantino** receives a massive 14% boost from a dynamic platoon edge, keeping him viable as our utility option. Meanwhile, **Jose Caballero** maintains a solid 63.85 score by capitalizing on a favorable platoon against Ranger Suarez, which outweighs the modest 6% penalty from facing a sub-4.00 xERA pitcher. We are keeping a close eye on **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland**, both of whom are projected as lower-order hitters against the weak Jack Kochanowicz; while the pitching matchup is favorable, their respective #8 and #9 spots limit their ceiling, keeping them in the marginal category.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves **Travis Bazzana**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a score of 50.93. While **Travis Bazzana** benefits from a premium leadoff spot, his base projection was ultimately cannibalized by the high performance of **Tyler Soderstrom**, who offers a much safer floor against Tatsuya Imai due to favorable platoon dynamics and a cleaner middle-of-the-order role. We are also wary of **Seiya Suzuki** and **Cole Young**, as both remain on the bubble; **Seiya Suzuki** faces a deceptively difficult matchup against Landen Roupp, and **Cole Young** is plagued by an unfavorable lineup spot that negates the benefit of his platoon edge. Monitor all \"Lineup Pending\" statuses closely, as any downward shift in order for **Gabriel Moreno** or **Brice Turang** could necessitate a pivot to the bench.",
